<speak>Thank you. I tend to write too much at the beginning and then wonder which part was important. For today, I've made separate headings for the review and the housekeeping matters. That should keep things tidy. I don't like mixing a note about a personal account with something about the company, even on the same page. The folders are separate as well. It saves me from wondering later whether a piece of correspondence belongs at home or at the office.</speak>